  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced capacities of constituents to create decent jobs, resilient livelihoods and employment-intensive approaches</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports the Government and social partners in Syria to promote employment-intensive approaches that generate decent jobs, strengthen livelihoods, and contribute to local recovery and resilience. Through inclusive Employment-Intensive Investment Programmes (EIIPs), the intervention combines short-term employment creation with infrastructure rehabilitation, skills development, and community-based recovery initiatives. Activities focus on vulnerable groups, including women, youth, returnees, and persons with disabilities, while integrating occupational safety and health standards, gender-responsive approaches, and local economic revitalization. The intervention also strengthens institutional capacities to design and implement sustainable labour market programmes that support transition from humanitarian response to long-term recovery and decent work.</narrative>
  </description>
